{
  "claim": "The Eiffel Tower can be 15 cm taller during summer.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.toureiffel.paris/en/news/history-and-culture/why-does-eiffel-tower-change-size",
      "title": "Why does the Eiffel Tower change size?",
      "publisher": "The Eiffel Tower (official website)",
      "snippet": "When temperatures rise, the Tower increases in size! This is a natural physical phenomenon called thermal expansion. Heat causes an increase in volume that makes the Eiffel Tower a few millimeters taller. The sun's movement over the course of a clear day can cause the top of the Tower to move in a circular curve measuring approximately 15 centimeters in diameter."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.snexplores.org/article/fun-facts-about-eiffel-tower",
      "title": "Fun facts about the Eiffel Tower",
      "publisher": "Science News Explores",
      "snippet": "Because heat causes the metal Tower to expand and cold causes it to shrink, the height of the Tower can vary with the outside temperature by 15 centimeters (5.9 inches)."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://theconversation.com/the-eiffel-tower-gets-bigger-every-summer-heres-why-261904",
      "title": "The Eiffel Tower gets bigger every summer – here's why",
      "publisher": "The Conversation",
      "snippet": "Specialists have estimated that the Eiffel Tower actually grows between 12 and 15 centimetres when comparing its size on cold winter days with the hottest days of summer."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.indiatoday.in/information/story/eiffel-tower-height-changes-thermal-expansion-iron-structure-seasonal-growth-2769543-2025-08-11",
      "title": "Why the Eiffel Tower appears taller in summer and what causes it",
      "publisher": "India Today",
      "snippet": "During the summer months, the Eiffel Tower can grow by as much as 15 centimetres (around 6 inches). Scientists and engineers can measure it accurately."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/eiffel-tower-grows-summer-shrinks-winter/",
      "title": "The Eiffel Tower Grows During Summers, Shrinks in Winters. Here's Why",
      "publisher": "Snopes",
      "snippet": "The Eiffel Tower does grow and contract in the summer and winter due to temperature fluctuations, according to its operators. However, the growth is only a few millimeters — not up to 6 inches. The 15-centimeter figure is actually the diameter of the curve the tower's top traces as it tilts away from the sun."
    }
  ]
}
